: #ff6600;\n            font-weight: bold;\n        }\n\n        .version-tag {\n            background-color: #fff5e6;\n            color: #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        .quote {\n            background-color: #f9f9f9;\n            border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;\n            padding: 8px 10px;\n            margin: 6px 0;\n            font-style: italic;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            color: #555555;\n        }\n\n        .quote-source {\n            display: block;\n            margin-top: 4px;\n            font-size: 10px;\n            color: #828282;\n            font-style: normal;\n        }\n\n        .update-type {\n            display: inline-block;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            font-size: 10px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-right: 4px;\n        }\n\n        .type-release {\n            background-color: #e6f7ff;\n            color: #0066cc;\n        }\n\n        .type-feature {\n            background-color: #e6ffe6;\n            color: #009900;\n        }\n\n        .type-bugfix {\n            background-color: #fff5e6;\n            color: #cc6600;\n        }\n\n        .topics {\n            margin-top: 6px;\n        }\n\n        footer {\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            padding: 15px;\n            text-align: center;\n            border-top: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            margin-top: 20px;\n        }\n\n        .footer-links {\n            font-size: 11px;\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .footer-links a {\n            color: #828282;\n            margin: 0 8px;\n        }\n\n        .footer-links a:hover {\n            color: #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        .insight-item {\n            margin-bottom: 12px;\n            padding-bottom: 10px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n        }\n\n        .insight-item:last-child {\n            border-bottom: none;\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n            padding-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        .insight-author {\n            font-size: 11px;\n            color: #828282;\n            margin-bottom: 3px;\n        }\n\n        .insight-source {\n            color: #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        @media print {\n            body {\n                background-color: #ffffff;\n            }\n\n            section {\n                break-inside: avoid;\n            }\n\n            .three-column-layout {\n                display: block;\n            }\n\n            section {\n                margin-bottom: 20px;\n                page-break-inside: avoid;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <div class=\"header-content\">\n            <div class=\"header-title\">Agentic Coding Research Report</div>\n            <div class=\"header-date\">2026-03-26</div>\n        </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n        <section class=\"new-products\">\n            <h2>New Products</h2>\n\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://mistral.ai/news/leanstral\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Leanstral</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    An open-source AI coding agent for Lean 4 formal proof engineering. Built by Mistral AI, enables 'trustworthy vibe-coding' by generating code with formal proofs. Achieves 26.3 points on FLTEval benchmark at 1/15th cost of Claude Sonnet 4.6. The 119B parameter model (6.5B active, 256k context) is Apache 2.0 licensed.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span class=\"tag source-tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag source-tag\">Show HN</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag source-tag\">Reddit</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag source-tag\">X</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n                    <span>Released: 2026-03-16</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"quote\">\n                    \"The formal verification angle is what makes this interesting. Most coding agents optimize for 'code that compiles and passes tests' — that's a low bar.\"\n                    <span class=\"quote-source\">Community Feedback</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"quote\">\n                    \"The big win here is you don't need to scrutinize the entire codebase — just the formal spec. That's a dramatically smaller review surface.\"\n                    <span class=\"quote-source\">Community Feedback</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n            <h2>Whitelist Updates</h2>\n\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <h3>Claude Code 2.1.77</h3>\n                <span class=\"update-type type-release\">Release</span>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    Stability improvements and capability enhancements for Claude Opus 4.6. March 2026 also introduced Voice Mode supporting 20 languages, remote control enhancements, and customizable keybindings.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span>2026-03-16</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n                    <a href=\"https://tjrobertson.com/anthropic-2026-claude-updates/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Release Notes</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"quote\">\n                    \"Claude Code generates cleaner, more shareable code compared to Codex which is better at reasoning\"\n                    <span class=\"quote-source\">Wall Street Journal</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <h3>Cursor 2.5</h3>\n                <span class=\"update-type type-release\">Release</span>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    Long-running agents for extended task handling and Composer 1.5. 2026 updates include improved tab completion with context-aware code suggestions that understand entire codebases.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span>2026-02-17</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n                    <a href=\"https://nerdleveltech.com/cursor-ai-editor-the-2026-developers-power-tool\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Release Notes</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <h3>GitHub Copilot</h3>\n                <span class=\"update-type type-release\">Release</span>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    Copilot SDK technical preview, GPT-5.2-Codex GA, and new agent mode with autonomous task planning. Visual Studio 2026 integration includes upgraded chat and language-aware symbol navigation.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span>2026-01-15</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n                    <a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/186497\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Release Notes</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"quote\">\n                    \"Copilot excels at boilerplate (76% acceptance rate) but struggles with debugging (12% acceptance rate)\"\n                    <span class=\"quote-source\">Production Testing Insights</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <h3>Gemini CLI</h3>\n                <span class=\"update-type type-feature\">Feature</span>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    'Plan mode' launch for complex research and migration planning tasks. Major nightly update brought UI polish, core fixes, chat resume footer, enhanced PTY support, and Google Cloud integration.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span>2026-03-11</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n                    <a href=\"https://releasebot.io/updates/google/gemini-cli\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Release Notes</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <h3>Codex CLI 26.228</h3>\n                <span class=\"update-type type-bugfix\">Bugfix</span>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    Performance improvements and bug fixes, including security fixes for CVE-2026-24842. Described as faster and more reliable with better real-time collaboration and autonomous task capabilities.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span>2026-02-28</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n                    <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog?type=codex-cli\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Release Notes</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <h3>Continue 1.26.0</h3>\n                <span class=\"update-type type-feature\">Feature</span>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    API key authentication for AWS Bedrock provider and OpenRouter API integration with Anthropic prompt caching support. 2026 updates focus on multi-model support and enhanced privacy features.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span>2026-02-20</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n                    <a href=\"https://newreleases.io/project/github/continuedev/continue/release/@continuedev%252Fconfig-yaml@1.26.0\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Release Notes</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n            <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n\n            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Mar/24/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Auto mode for Claude Code</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                    <span class=\"insight-source\">Simon Willison</span> <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> Blog <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> 2026-03-24\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    Anthropic introduced 'auto mode' where Claude makes permission decisions with safeguards. Claude Sonnet 4.6 acts as classifier to review actions before execution.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"tag\">AI</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Mar/24/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Package Managers Need Cooldowns After LiteLLM Attack</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                    <span class=\"insight-source\">Simon Willison</span> <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> Blog <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> 2026-03-24\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    Following LiteLLM supply chain attack, advocates for dependency cooldowns. Major tools now support minimum release age features to prevent malicious packages.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">supply-chain</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">python</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">PyPI</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Mar/24/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Streaming Experts: Running Massive LLMs on Consumer Hardware</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                    <span class=\"insight-source\">Simon Willison</span> <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> Blog <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> 2026-03-24\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    'Streaming experts' technique allows running larger MoE models on hardware without enough RAM. Running Qwen3.5-397B in 48GB RAM, 1T parameter models on MacBook Pro.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"tag\">AI</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">local-LLMs</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">Qwen</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">optimization</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Mar/12/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">AI-Assisted Coding Exposes Developer Divide</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                    <span class=\"insight-source\">Les Orchard (via Simon Willison)</span> <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> Blog <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> 2026-03-12\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    AI-assisted coding revealing split between 'craft-lovers' and 'make-it-go' developers. Choice makes visible underlying motivation for why people got into programming.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"tag\">AI</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">careers</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">generative-ai</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">LLMs</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Mar/12/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">NYT Magazine: Coding After Coders</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                    <span class=\"insight-source\">Clive Thompson (via Simon Willison)</span> <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> Blog <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> 2026-03-12\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    Comprehensive piece interviewed 70+ developers about AI-assisted development. Programming has unique advantage: code can be tested to verify correctness.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"tag\">AI</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">careers</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">generative-ai</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">press-quotes</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/09/anthropic-launches-code-review-tool-to-check-flood-of-ai-generated-code/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Launches Code Review Tool</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                    <span class=\"insight-source\">Rebecca Bellan</span> <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> TechMedia <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> 2026-03-09\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    Multi-agent system automatically analyzes AI-generated code and flags logic errors. Uses multiple AI agents working in parallel, $15-25 per review on average.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"tag\">AI</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">code-review</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">multi-agent-systems</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/24/openai-adds-open-source-tools-to-help-developers-build-for-teen-safety/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Teen Safety Open Source Tools</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                    <span class=\"insight-source\">Amanda Silberling</span> <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> TechMedia <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> 2026-03-24\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    Open-source prompts for making AI apps safer for teens. Addresses graphic violence, sexual content, harmful body ideals, dangerous activities, age-restricted goods.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"tag\">AI</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">safety</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">teen-safety</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/25/apple-overhauls-its-app-developer-platform-with-100-new-metrics-more-tools/\" class=\"accent-link\" target=\"_blank\">Apple Overhauls App Developer Platform</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                    <span class=\"insight-source\">Sarah Perez</span> <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> TechMedia <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span> 2026-03-25\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-description\">\n                    App Store Connect update adds 100+ new metrics for monetization, subscriptions, user behavior. First-party insights based on Apple's actual data rather than estimates.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"tag\">Apple</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">developers</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">app-store</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag\">analytics</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </section>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <div class=\"footer-links\">\n            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">GitHub</a>\n            <span>© 2026 Agentic Coding Research Report</span>\n        </div>\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>"
